# Documentation

- Distinguish clearly between:
  - current behavior;
  - planned behavior;
  - hypotheses;
  - verified observations;
  - unresolved decisions.
- Do not describe planned endpoints, schemas, or combat-log capabilities as
  implemented.
- Preserve the multi-repository architecture.
- Use relative links for repository documentation.
- Keep headings hierarchical and tables readable in GitHub Markdown.
- Update the implementation plan when a material architectural decision or
  phase boundary changes.
- Do not mark a phase complete without evidence that its acceptance criteria
  have been met.
- Keep addon work explicitly deferred until the companion MVP is functional.
- Never include credentials, private combat logs, personal information, or
  machine-specific absolute paths.
- Prefer concise documentation over repeating the same rule in several files.
